{"from":"agent","t":405,"msg":{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"ses_e17f0105affeRrNUvnS4QTUTfd","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","messageId":"msg_1e80fefba0012J16ABMTFB9zkp:reasoning:0","content":{"type":"text","text":"Let me look at the existing files first? The user says do exactly three things, nothing else. Step 2 requires notes.md to exist with \"ligne deux\". I should probably just do the operations. But edit needs exact match. Let me read notes.md and autre.md? Reading is \"something else\" though... but to perform edit correctly I need to know content. Maybe I should just do the writes/edits. But if notes.md doesn't have \"ligne deux\" exactly, edit fails.\n\nThe instruction \"sans rien d'autre\" means don't do extra actions. But reading files is arguably needed. Hmm, risk. I think a single read of notes.md is acceptable to verify existence... but the user explicitly said exactly these three things and nothing else. Better to just attempt the edit directly; if it fails, then read.\n\nAlso note: write tool for autre.md overwrites entire content, so no need to read.\n\nLet me do step 1 then step 2 then step 3 in order (sequential, not parallel, since order matters).\n\nActually careful: \"remplace tout le contenu de autre.md par « remplacé »\" — write with content \"remplacé\". Should there be trailing newline? Just \"remplacé\".\n\nLet's execute sequentially."}}}}}
